{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438837-how-do-you-discourage-players-from-gaming-harmony-using-junk-food","id":1438837,"title":"How do you discourage players from gaming Harmony using junk food?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-09T16:30:46-08:00","id":1438837,"title":"How do you discourage players from gaming Harmony using junk food?","content":"Overall I really like how 2E Harmony is something you have to keep in balance, but it seems very vulnerable to some very silly exploits. Like, oops, I just ate an orphan for essence and broke toward Spirit. Better pop open a bag of Cheetos so I can break back to Flesh again. I've dubbed this the &quot;Bag of Cheetos&quot; problem in my group and I'm curious how other groups handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4953-asatj","name":"AsaTJ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4953_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T17:24:45-08:00","id":1438848,"title":"","content":"Eating processed food only helps if you're at Harmony 3 or below. At that point you have at least two bans that could keep you from eating easy food like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T19:16:10-08:00","id":1438866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AsaTJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438837-how-do-you-discourage-players-from-gaming-harmony-using-junk-food#post1438837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, oops, I just ate an orphan for essence and broke toward Spirit. Better pop open a bag of Cheetos so I can break back to Flesh again.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2022 As nofather points out, unless you're Harmony 3 or below, that's not even giving you a chance to rebalance, and even when it does it's only back up to the point where you have a single Ban.<br /> \u2022 Unless you're Primal Urge 1 you are deriving no benefit from eating processed food that isn't meat (and even processed food that <i>is</i> meat, at 4 and above), and otherwise you're only getting to make a roll that a character with average Attributes and no Touchstone bonus will generally succeed at three times out of four.<br /> \u2022 Processed food literally does not grow on trees and if your character is at the level of Harmony where they can drop into the Shadow from the Flesh without a locus but not vice-versa then sources of it may be hard to come by.<br /> \u2022 The same category of breaking points toward flesh that eating processed food occupies includes <i>staying out of the Shadow for one day</i>, which likewise only gets you out of the bottom of the scale on a successful roll.<br /> \u2022 Breaking towards the opposite half of the scale is exactly as easy for any given character as it is for them to fall into Hard Rage, Touchstone bonus notwithstanding, and the contributing Attributes directly reduce the effectiveness of mind-altering powers used against the character. A werewolf character that can easily rebalance is a volatile one.<br /> <br /> Unless you're uselessly dedicating camera time to characters gorging on useless food to dig out of the hole they've put themselves in, this is a comparative non-issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T19:23:07-08:00","id":1438870,"title":"","content":"I think nofather and Satchel have answered the question fairly well, so I just have a question of my own. It may sound rhetorical but it's genuine curiosity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AsaTJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438837-how-do-you-discourage-players-from-gaming-harmony-using-junk-food#post1438837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've dubbed this the &quot;Bag of Cheetos&quot; problem in my group</div> </div> </div> </div>Has this actually emerged with your group in play as a problem, or has it only come up in theorycrafting conversations about hypotheticals?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T20:15:31-08:00","id":1438876,"title":"","content":"It's mostly theoretical. Like, would all werewolves carry junk food with them to get back in balance, given the logic of this universe? I haven't seen anyone abuse it yet. I just wanted to make sure I understood the rules, since it seems too easy. The &quot;atonement&quot; (eat a cheeseburger) doesn't have the same narrative weight as the &quot;crime&quot; (eating a human being).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4953-asatj","name":"AsaTJ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4953_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-09T20:29:36-08:00","id":1438880,"title":"","content":"I mean it's an RP thing for the most part. You can loose humanity as a Vampire by just watching someone eat a meal but it's not like that's going to come up unless someone's doing it to make a point. <br /> <br /> Likewise, a person that low harmony might not WANT to eat processed food, and might need to get coerced or forced. It's not as simple as just &quot;Oh my harmony is 3 lemme go eat a cheeseburger&quot; because it's generally assumed that the numerical stats aren't actually acknowledged in-universe besides vague &quot;My Harmony is low.&quot; &quot;I'm closer to the spirit-side&quot;, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T08:24:33-08:00","id":1438942,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve yet to actually play Werewolf, so this is to be taken with a boulder of salt, but my reading of the Harmony system is that in order to stay at either extreme of Harmony, you, the player, have to make a concerted effort to do so. It seems devised that, all else being equal, the breaking points will tend to send you back into the 4-7 range eventually. As already brought up, simply staying out of the Shadow for a day can bring you back to Harmony 4. On the flip side, you can lose high Harmony simply by avoiding your pack. So yes, eating Cheetos will help ground in in humanity if you are way too close to spirit. But so will other pretty mundane things. I get the impression that the intent is less \u201ceat Cheetos to regain Harmony\u201d and more \u201cif you are intentionally roleplaying a low Harmony character, avoid Cheetos.\u201d This is reflected in-universe, at least in extreme cases, as Shunned by the Moon makes it clear that most Zi\u2019ir are the result of deliberately neglecting one\u2019s Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T10:55:17-08:00","id":1438972,"title":"","content":"Basically, carrying around a bag of junk food isn't going to work well enough to be a thing. It's not like being diabetic and making sure you have both a candy bar and some insulin on you for emergencies. Getting back towards balance from the extremes isn't difficult, but it's not instant either. It takes enough time and intent that you need a bit more than just popping some chips in your mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-10T16:40:02-08:00","id":1439061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AsaTJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438837-how-do-you-discourage-players-from-gaming-harmony-using-junk-food?p=1438876#post1438876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;atonement&quot; (eat a cheeseburger) doesn't have the same narrative weight as the &quot;crime&quot; (eating a human being).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not meant to. Harmony is, to a degree, self-balancing. When more constant deeds push you further and further towards the spirit, you reach a crisis point where your imbalance becomes extremely unhealthy. Even mild nods towards the flesh are then able to pull you back from the brink, though they may be increasingly difficult to perform in the condition you've driven yourself toward. When the flesh is starving, even a small meal is better than nothing at all. The same applies to cleaving too closely to the flesh. When your Harmony enters crisis, you're not trapped in that crisis. More lenient triggers become available to pull you back.<br /> <br /> 2e Harmony isn't a slippery slope where the farther down you fall the harder it is to climb back up. Crises of imbalance happen to really unwise werewolves, ideologically extreme werewolves, or werewolves in extreme situations. Harmony is more like hygeine: a spiritual health regime you need to moderate and mind and keep up on. Don't forget to hunt. Neither isolate yourself in the <i>Hisil</i> nor forget it to concentrate on the ways of humanity and flesh. The pressure of Harmony is the pressure to stay liminal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-21T19:18:22-07:00","id":1440892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AsaTJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1438837-how-do-you-discourage-players-from-gaming-harmony-using-junk-food?p=1438876#post1438876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;atonement&quot; (eat a cheeseburger) doesn't have the same narrative weight as the &quot;crime&quot; (eating a human being).</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect Forsaken will regard eating a human as a crime not because it's a breaking point towards the spirit side, but because it's a violation of the Oath of the Moon. And what's going to be required as an atonement for that in the eyes of one's fellows and the Lunes probably will actually have to be more proportionate.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it seems as though there are forms of murdering humans that are Harmony breaking points, but that werewolf culture will be totally unconcerned with (assuming that the person in question wasn't actual prey in the Sacred Hunt).<br /> <br /> Otherwise, as has been said, it's bringing the wrong mindset to view the sides in terms of crime and atonement. Like, I doubt you're atoning your way into the point where shapeshifting becomes violent and painful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T20:59:08-07:00","id":1445921,"title":"","content":"Harmony seems to be something that's constantly shifting, especially at the extremes. A Uratha who finds himself falling too far toward spirit would be wise to go invest in his human side, whether that's going out to the movies, snacking on junk food, wasting time on video games, or whatever keeps him feeling human.<br /> <br /> As said earlier, carrying around a bag of cheetos wouldn't do it, a wolf far in spirit needs to go engage anything at all to remind him that he's partially human.<br /> <br /> This isn't like a Vampire's Humanity or a Mage's Wisdom that spirals slowly down and requires concerted effort to raise. Harmony is just a day-to-day part of a Uratha's life that goes up and down like moods or habits. Keeping Harmony in balance is like reminding yourself to stay hydrated. Nothing is &quot;OP&quot; when it comes to moving it in either direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26294-chris_john","name":"Chris_John","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T02:26:38-07:00","id":1445945,"title":"","content":"I think food in particular needs to consider the effect of Primal Urge on diet.<br /> <br /> Sure, the fact that an Uratha past a fairly low threshold won't derive nutrition from it doesn't strictly mean it isn't pleasant to eat, but it can be worth considering for roleplaying purposes whether a particular werewolf would be inclined towards that kind of breaking point for Flesh. At the very least, there could be wider personality implications for choosing to ground oneself in food that does not state hunger rather than some human interaction.<br /> <br /> Mind, a given pack or tribal gathering might lean into it; eating junk food might fit symbolically as a way of both pushing Harmony closer to one side and atoning for (minor) cannibalism if that's <i>all</i> you're permitted to eat for a period and under circumstances that make it a fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}